<section className="faqs bg-aurora">
        <div className="aurora-blob aurora-blob-1"></div>
        <div className="aurora-blob aurora-blob-2"></div>
        <div className="aurora-blob aurora-blob-3"></div>
        <h2>Motion Graphics Course <span className="cc-highlight">FAQs</span></h2>
        <p className="faqDetails">Short answers to common questions about the course, creative careers and what you build during training.</p>
        <div className="faq-grid">
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>What is motion graphics?</summary>
                    <p>Motion graphics brings graphic design to life: text, logos, icons and shapes are animated to share a message or build a brand. Unlike character animation, it is design-led.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>What will I learn in this motion graphics course?</summary>
                    <p>Design principles, Photoshop, Illustrator, storyboarding, After Effects, kinetic typography, logo animation, explainer videos, 3D basics, UI motion and Gen AI tools, ending with a showreel.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>Do I need design or animation experience?</summary>
                    <p>No. The course starts with design basics before any software, and every tool is taught from the first click.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>Why is After Effects so important?</summary>
                    <p>After Effects is the industry-standard tool for motion graphics. Almost every motion graphic designer job asks for it, so it is the main tool of this course.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>What is kinetic typography?</summary>
                    <p>Animated text that moves in sync with music or voiceover. It is used in Reels, ads, explainer videos and title sequences.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>Is this a motion graphic designer course for jobs in Delhi?</summary>
                    <p>Yes. It is a job-focused motion graphic designer course, taught at our Greater Kailash II campus in South Delhi, and every batch is also available online.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>Is there a motion graphics course online?</summary>
                    <p>Yes. You can join the motion graphics course online or offline, with the same live classes, projects and placement support.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>How is it different from the Graphic Design &amp; Video Editing course?</summary>
                    <p>Both share a design foundation. This course focuses on animation in After Effects, while the video editing course focuses on editing footage in Premiere Pro.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>How is Gen AI used in the course?</summary>
                    <p>AI tools are used in every module, and a dedicated module on motion graphics with Gen AI covers ChatGPT, Adobe Firefly and AI tools for animation, voice and subtitles.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>What is a showreel and will I make one?</summary>
                    <p>A showreel is a 60 to 90 second video of your best motion work, and it is what employers watch first. Yes, you build one in the final module.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>What jobs can I get after the course?</summary>
                    <p>Motion Graphic Designer, Graphic Designer, Brand Animator, Explainer Video Designer, Social Media Motion Designer, or freelance motion work.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>Do you provide placement support?</summary>
                    <p>Yes. This motion graphics design course comes with 100% Placement Assistance: showreel review, Behance setup, mock interviews and referrals through our 250+ hiring partners. Top performers can get a paid in-house internship.</p>
                </details>
                            <details className="faq slide-up-section">
                    <summary>What certificates will I get?</summary>
                    <p>10+ certificates, including the DizitalAdda certificate in graphic design and motion graphics, Skill India recognition and a certificate for each live project.</p>
                </details>
                    </div>
    </section>


    
